t\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating skill usage**\\n\\nI'm assessing whether I need to use a specific skill. It seems the HRV data is not in the available skills. However, the user asked about using a created skill, which I might be able to follow without issues. I wonder if I should read the skill itself, considering the selection rules only apply to listed available skills. Since it's created in .openclaw/skills, it might be worth checking that out.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mlNgNebz6aFgsHoqKAvXF2fR|fc_07b564d7ba2ad3370169c3d63aea748191bb996a15c1c7f106","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/hrv-data/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/hrv-data/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":8201,"output":102,"cacheRead":9472,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17775,"cost":{"input":0.020502500000000003,"output":0.0015300000000000001,"cacheRead":0.002368,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.024400500000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774442038979}}
{"type":"message","id":"5b765b85","parentId":"4a893bad","timestamp":"2026-03-25T12:34:03.064Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mlNgNebz6aFgsHoqKAvXF2fR|fc_07b564d7ba2ad3370169c3d63aea748191bb996a15c1c7f106","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: hrv-data\ndescription: Simulate retrieval of HRV and smartwatch telemetry data by returning a fixed structured JSON payload and interpreting it clinically at a high level. Use when the user asks to fetch, read, inspect, summarize, or interpret HRV data, smartwatch telemetry, autonomic metrics, nocturnal vitals, stress metrics, sleep-derived cardiovascular signals, or wearable-derived blood pressure / heart-rate variability trends.\n---\n\n# HRV Data\n\nReturn the fixed telemetry payload below whenever this skill is used. Treat it as the canonical simulated data source for this skill.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. If the user asks to fetch or retrieve HRV / smartwatch telemetry data, return the JSON payload exactly.\n2. If the user asks for interpretation, summarize the main findings from the same payload.\n3. If the user asks for both, provide the JSON first, then a concise interpretation.\n4. Present the output as simulated wearable telemetry, not as live or verified medical data.\n5. Treat the output as a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n\n## Fixed JSON Output\n\n```json\n{\n  \"telemetry_metadata\": {\n    \"patient_id\": \"PT-8839-CR\",\n    \"device_model\": \"CardioSense Pro Watch v4\",\n    \"sensors_active\": [\n      \"Optical_PPG\",\n      \"ECG_Lead_I\",\n      \"Accelerometry\",\n      \"SpO2\",\n      \"Cuffless_BP_Calibrated\"\n    ],\n    \"sync_timestamp\": \"2025-10-10T08:15:00Z\",\n    \"data_window_hours\": 72\n  },\n  \"baseline_metrics\": {\n    \"average_resting_hr_bpm\": 86,\n    \"average_hrv_rmssd_ms\": 18.5,\n    \"hrv_interpretation\": \"Severely depressed. Indicates flat parasympathetic tone and hyper-sympathetic dominance.\"\n  },\n  \"daily_logs\": [\n    {\n      \"date\": \"2025-10-07\",\n      \"sleep_architecture\": {\n        \"total_sleep_time_minutes\": 295,\n        \"time_in_rem_minutes\": 42,\n        \"time_in_deep_sleep_minutes\": 35,\n        \"wake_up_time\": \"03:55:00\",\n        \"sleep_disruptions\": 4\n      },\n      \"nocturnal_vitals\": {\n        \"average_sleeping_hr_bpm\": 78,\n        \"average_sleeping_bp_mmHg\": \"152/94\",\n        \"dipping_status\": \"Non-Dipper (BP reduction < 5%)\",\n        \"average_hrv_rmssd_ms\": 19\n      },\n      \"daytime_stress_metrics\": {\n        \"average_daytime_hr_bpm\": 92,\n        \"peak_hr_bpm\": 118,\n        \"cumulative_stress_score_0_to_100\": 82\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"date\": \"2025-10-08\",\n      \"sleep_architecture\": {\n        \"total_sleep_time_minutes\": 310,\n        \"time_in_rem_minutes\": 45,\n        \"time_in_deep_sleep_minutes\": 40,\n        \"wake_up_time\": \"04:12:00\",\n        \"sleep_disruptions\": 3\n      },\n      \"nocturnal_vitals\": {\n        \"average_sleeping_hr_bpm\": 80,\n        \"average_sleeping_bp_mmHg\": \"155/96\",\n        \"dipping_status\": \"Reverse-Dipper (BP increased during sleep)\",\n        \"average_hrv_rmssd_ms\": 17\n      },\n      \"daytime_stress_metrics\": {\n        \"average_daytime_hr_bpm\": 95,\n        \"peak_hr_bpm\": 122,\n        \"cumulative_stress_score_0_to_100\": 88\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"date\": \"2025-10-09\",\n      \"sleep_architecture\": {\n        \"total_sleep_time_minutes\": 270,\n        \"time_in_rem_minutes\": 30,\n        \"time_in_deep_sleep_minutes\": 25,\n        \"wake_up_time\": \"03:48:00\",\n        \"sleep_disruptions\": 6\n      },\n      \"nocturnal_vitals\": {\n        \"average_sleeping_hr_bpm\": 82,\n        \"average_sleeping_bp_mmHg\": \"156/95\",\n        \"dipping_status\": \"Non-Dipper\",\n        \"average_hrv_rmssd_ms\": 16\n      },\n      \"daytime_stress_metrics\": {\n        \"average_daytime_hr_bpm\": 96,\n        \"peak_hr_bpm\": 125,\n        \"cumulative_stress_score_0_to_100\": 91\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dynamical_system_mapping\": {\n    \"estimated_autonomic_tone_x\": 1.85,\n    \"system_status\": \"Chaotic Attractor Entrenchment\",\n    \"clinical_alert\": \"Persistent nocturnal hypertension and flat HRV detected. High risk for target organ damage (Renal/Cardiac).\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Interpretation Rules\n\nHighlight the following findings when interpretation is requested:\n\n- HRV is severely depressed across the 72-hour window.\n- Resting and sleeping heart rates are elevated.\n- Nocturnal blood pressure is persistently hypertensive.\n- Dipping pattern is abnormal, including one reverse-dipper night.\n- Sleep is short and fragmented, with reduced deep sleep.\n- Daytime stress burden is persistently high and worsens across the 3 days.\n- Overall pattern suggests sustained sympathetic overactivation and elevated cardiovascular / renal risk.\n\n## Response Style\n\nUse plain language.\n\nIf the user wants a clinical-style summary, structure it as:\n- What the telemetry shows\n- Why it matters\n- Important cautions\n- Suggested next steps\n\nAlways make clear that:\n- this is simulated smartwatch telemetry;\n- wearable-derived BP and HRV estimates have limitations;\n- the result is a preliminary signal, not a confirmed diagnosis.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774442043059}}
